@@ -1,3 +1,16 @@
+pve-cluster (9.1.7+supermox2) trixie; urgency=medium
+
+  * debian: init.d/pve-cluster seeds /etc/pve/storage.cfg. pmxcfs creates that
+    file empty and no package in this tree ever fills it, so a clean node booted
+    with no storage defined at all: `pct create`, the web UI's Create CT and
+    `pvesm list local` then failed with "volume 'local:...' does not exist" or
+    "unknown storage". The script writes the single-node `dir: local` stanza
+    under /var/lib/vz once, only after /etc/pve is mounted and only while no
+    storage is defined yet, so an admin's or a cluster's storage.cfg is never
+    touched.
+
+ -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 05:50:46 -0800
+
